(527,1155,'Tumors or cancer of the THYROID GLAND.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:04',NULL,NULL,'14752FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(528,1156,'A fungal infection that may appear in two forms: 1) a primary lesion characterized by the formation of a small cutaneous nodule and small nodules along the lymphatics that may heal within several months; and 2) chronic granulomatous lesions characterized by thick crusts, warty growths, and unusual vascularity and infection in the middle or upper lobes of the lung.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:05',NULL,NULL,'14639FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(529,1158,'A form of LEPROSY in which there are clinical manifestations of both principal types (lepromatous and tuberculoid). The disease may shift toward one of these two polar or principal forms.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:05',NULL,NULL,'14597FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(530,1160,'Sexually transmitted form of anogenital warty growth caused by the human papillomaviruses.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:05',NULL,NULL,'5922FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(531,1161,'A syndrome produced by severe protein deficiency, characterized by retarded growth, changes in skin and hair pigment, edema, and pathologic changes in the liver, including fatty infiltration, necrosis, and fibrosis. The word is a local name in Gold Coast, Africa, meaning &quot;displaced child&quot;. Although first reported from Africa, kwashiorkor is now known throughout the world, but mainly in the tropics and subtropics. It is considered to be related to marasmus. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:05',NULL,NULL,'5782FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(532,1163,'A localized infection of mucous membranes or skin caused by toxigenic strains of CORYNEBACTERIUM DIPHTHERIAE. It is characterized by the presence of a pseudomembrane at the site of infection. DIPHTHERIA TOXIN, produced by C. diphtheriae, can cause myocarditis, polyneuritis, and other systemic toxic effects.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:06',NULL,NULL,'5682FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(533,1164,'Infections or infestations with parasitic organisms. They are often contracted through contact with an intermediate vector, but may occur as the result of direct exposure.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:06',NULL,NULL,'5676FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(534,1165,'Acute, localized autoinoculable infectious disease usually acquired through sexual contact. Caused by HAEMOPHILUS DUCREYI, it occurs endemically almost worldwide, especially in tropical and subtropical countries and more commonly in seaports and urban areas than in rural areas.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:06',NULL,NULL,'14187FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(535,1166,'Scaly papule or warty growth, caused by five fungi, that spreads as a result of satellite lesions affecting the foot or leg. The extremity may become swollen and, at its distal portion, covered with various nodular, tumorous, verrucous lesions that resemble cauliflower. In rare instances, the disease may begin on the hand or wrist and involve the entire upper extremity. (Arnold, Odom, and James, Andrew&#39;s Diseases of the Skin, 8th ed, p362)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:06',NULL,NULL,'14103FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(536,1167,'Syphilis acquired in utero and manifested by any of several characteristic tooth (Hutchinson&#39;s teeth) or bone malformations and by active mucocutaneous syphilis at birth or shortly thereafter. Ocular and neurologic changes may also occur.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:07',NULL,NULL,'5483FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(537,1168,'An inflammatory disease of the liver caused by hepatitis C virus lasting six months or more.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:07',NULL,NULL,'14037FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(538,1169,'Paludisme Falciparum','fr',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:07',NULL,NULL,'5339FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(539,1169,'Malaria caused by PLASMODIUM FALCIPARUM. This is the severest form of malaria and is associated with the highest levels of parasites in the blood. This disease is characterized by irregularly recurring febrile paroxysms that in extreme cases occur with acute cerebral, renal, or gastrointestinal manifestations.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:07',NULL,NULL,'5338FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(540,1172,'The lack of sufficient energy or protein to meet the body&#39;s metabolic demands, as a result of either an inadequate dietary intake of protein, intake of poor quality dietary protein, increased demands due to disease, or increased nutrient losses.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:08',NULL,NULL,'4745FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(541,1173,'Infection with CYTOMEGALOVIRUS, characterized by enlarged cells bearing intranuclear inclusions. Infection may be in almost any organ, but the salivary glands are the most common site in children, as are the lungs in adults.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:08',NULL,NULL,'13363FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(542,1174,'Infeccion aguda febril','es',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:08',NULL,NULL,'15962FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(543,1176,'A genus of gram-negative, facultatively anaerobic, rod-shaped bacteria that utilizes citrate as a sole carbon source. It is pathogenic for humans, causing enteric fevers, gastroenteritis, and bacteremia. Food poisoning is the most common clinical manifestation. Organisms within this genus are separated on the basis of antigenic characteristics, sugar fermentation patterns, and bacteriophage susceptibility.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:09',NULL,NULL,'4687FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(544,1177,'Tumors or cancer of the UTERUS.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:09',NULL,NULL,'4572FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(545,1178,'An acute form of TUBERCULOSIS in which minute tubercles are formed in a number of organs of the body due to dissemination of the bacilli through the blood stream.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:09',NULL,NULL,'4458FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(546,1179,'A disseminated vesicular-pustular eruption caused by the herpes simplex virus (HERPESVIRUS HOMINUS), the VACCINIA VIRUS, or Varicella zoster (HERPESVIRUS 3, HUMAN). It is usually superimposed on a preexisting, inactive or active, atopic dermatitis (DERMATITIS, ATOPIC).','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:09',NULL,NULL,'12915FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(547,1180,'A mild, highly infectious viral disease of children, characterized by vesicular lesions in the mouth and on the hands and feet. It is caused by COXSACKIEVIRUSES A.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:10',NULL,NULL,'12830FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(548,1181,'An acute infection of the skin caused by species of STREPTOCOCCUS. This disease most frequently affects infants, young children, and the elderly. Characteristics include pink-to-red lesions that spread rapidly and are warm to the touch. The commonest site of involvement is the face.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:10',NULL,NULL,'12764FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(549,1182,'A respiratory infection caused by BORDETELLA PERTUSSIS and characterized by paroxysmal coughing ending in a prolonged crowing intake of breath.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:10',NULL,NULL,'3947FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(550,1183,'An acute infectious disease caused by YERSINIA PESTIS that affects humans, wild rodents, and their ectoparasites. This condition persists due to its firm entrenchment in sylvatic rodent-flea ecosystems throughout the world. Bubonic plague is the most common form.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:10',NULL,NULL,'3918FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(551,1184,'A contagious skin disease caused by a parasitic mite (Sarcoptes scabiei) and characterized by intense itching.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:10',NULL,NULL,'139FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(552,1185,'Tumors or cancer of the either the COLON or RECTUM or both. The most frequent malignant tumor in the United States. Etiological factors which increase the risk of colorectal cancer include chronic ulcerative colitis, familial polyposis of the colon, exposure to asbestos, irradiation of the cervix.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:11',NULL,NULL,'3782FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(553,1186,'Poisoning caused by ingestion of food harboring species of SALMONELLA. Conditions of raising, shipping, slaughtering, and marketing of domestic animals contribute to the spread of this bacterium in the food supply.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:11',NULL,NULL,'3581FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
