(610,1267,'A syndrome characterized by cardiac enlargement and congestive heart failure. It probably represents the end result of many forms of myocardial damage produced by a variety of toxic, metabolic, or infectious agents.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:26',NULL,NULL,'13597FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(611,1272,'General term for cysts and cystic diseases of the ovary.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:27',NULL,NULL,'13469FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(612,1273,'A chronic, progressive dermatosis characterized by boardlike hardening and immobility of the affected skin, with visceral involvement, especially of lungs, esophagus, kidneys and heart. It may be accompanied by calcinosis, Raynaud&#39;s phenomenon, and telangiectasis (CREST syndrome). It includes acrosclerosis and sclerodactyly.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:28',NULL,NULL,'13444FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(613,1287,'A form of lupus erythematosus in which the skin may be the only organ involved or in which skin involvement precedes the spread into other body systems. It has been classified into three forms - acute (= LUPUS ERYTHEMATOSUS, SYSTEMIC with skin lesions), subacute, and chronic (= LUPUS ERYTHEMATOSUS, DISCOID).','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:30',NULL,NULL,'13400FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(614,1288,'A hair-containing cyst or sinus, occurring chiefly in the coccygeal region.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:30',NULL,NULL,'13382FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(615,1289,'A true cyst of the pancreas to be distinguished from the much more common PANCREATIC PSEUDOCYST by possessing a mucous epithelial lining. Pancreatic cysts are categorized as congenital, retention, neoplastic, parasitic, enterogenous, or dermoid. Congenital cysts occur more frequently as solitary cysts but may be multiple. Retention cysts are gross enlargements of pancreatic ducts secondary to ductal obstruction. (From Bockus Gastroenterology, 4th ed, p4145)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:30',NULL,NULL,'13377FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(616,1291,'Infection with CYTOMEGALOVIRUS, characterized by enlarged cells bearing intranuclear inclusions. Infection may be in almost any organ, but the salivary glands are the most common site in children, as are the lungs in adults.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:30',NULL,NULL,'13365FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(617,1292,'Gallbladder or biliary duct problems not specified.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:07:31',NULL,NULL,'8FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
