(1316,2760,'Inflammation of the endometrium. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:36',NULL,NULL,'4887FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1317,2763,'Inflammation of the joint space(s).','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:36',NULL,NULL,'4881FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1318,2764,'Abnormal protrusion of the intestine into the inguinal canal.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:36',NULL,NULL,'4877FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1319,2768,'Dysfunction of one or more cranial nerves causally related to a traumatic injury. Penetrating and nonpenetrating CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; NECK INJURIES; and trauma to the facial region are conditions associated with cranial nerve injuries.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:37',NULL,NULL,'4873FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1320,2772,'This concept includes injury of liver or gallbladder','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:38',NULL,NULL,'17101FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1321,2779,'Bleeding into a cerebral hemisphere of the brain, including lobar, subcortical white matter, and basal ganglia hemorrhages. Commonly associated conditions include HYPERTENSION; INTRACRANIAL ARTERIOSCLEROSIS; INTRACRANIAL ANEURYSM; CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; INTRACRANIAL ARTERIOVENOUS MALFORMATIONS; CEREBRAL AMYLOID ANGIOPATHY; and CEREBRAL INFARCTION.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:39',NULL,NULL,'4828FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1322,2781,'Uterine bleeding, usually irregular or acyclic, between periods.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:39',NULL,NULL,'4805FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1323,2784,'Injuries to tissues caused by contact with heat, steam, chemicals (BURNS, CHEMICAL), electricity (BURNS, ELECTRIC), or the like.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:39',NULL,NULL,'4775FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1324,2785,'Symmetrical osteitis of the four limbs, chiefly localized to the phalanges and the terminal epiphyses of the long bones of the forearm and leg, sometimes extending to the proximal ends of the limbs and the flat bones, and accompanied by dorsal kyphosis and joint involvement. It is often secondary to chronic conditions of the lungs and heart. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:40',NULL,NULL,'4757FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1325,2786,'Calculi occurring in the kidney. Calculi too large to pass spontaneously range in size from 1 cm to the staghorn stones that occupy the renal pelvis and calyces.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:40',NULL,NULL,'4753FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1326,2787,'Abnormally increased convexity in the curvature of the thoracic spine as viewed from the side. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:40',NULL,NULL,'4743FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1327,2788,'Disturbances in sexual desire and the psychophysiologic changes that characterize the sexual response cycle and cause marked distress and interpersonal difficulty. (APA, DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:40',NULL,NULL,'4737FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1328,2789,'Increase in the mass of bone per unit volume.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:40',NULL,NULL,'4730FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1329,2794,'A syndrome characterized by persistent or recurrent fatigue, diffuse musculoskeletal pain, sleep disturbances, and subjective cognitive impairment of 6 months duration or longer. Symptoms are not caused by ongoing exertion; are not relieved by rest; and result in a substantial reduction of previous levels of occupational, educational, social, or personal activities. Minor alterations of immune, neuroendocrine, and autonomic function may be associated with this syndrome. There is also considerable overlap between this condition and FIBROMYALGIA. (From Semin Neurol 1998;18(2):237-42; Ann Intern Med 1994 Dec 15;121(12): 953-9)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:41',NULL,NULL,'4710FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1330,2795,'A chronic, atrophic skin disease characterized by white, angular, flat, well-defined, indurated papules with an erythematous halo and follicular, black, keratotic plugs. It is the most common cause of kraurosis vulvae in females and balanitis xerotica obliterans in males. It is called also white spot disease and Csillag&#39;s disease. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:41',NULL,NULL,'4702FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1331,2797,'Fibrous, bony, cartilaginous and osteocartilaginous fragments in a synovial joint. Major causes are osteochondritis dissecans, synovial chondromatosis, osteophytes, fractured articular surfaces and damaged menisci.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:42',NULL,NULL,'4682FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1332,2798,'The anterior concavity in the curvature of the lumbar and cervical spine as viewed from the side. The term usually refers to abnormally increased curvature (hollow back, saddle back, swayback). It does not include lordosis as normal mating posture in certain animals ( = POSTURE + SEX BEHAVIOR, ANIMAL).','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:42',NULL,NULL,'4681FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1333,2800,'Leukemia associated with hyperplasia and overactivity of the lymphoid tissue. There are increased numbers of circulating malignant lymphocytes and lymphoblasts. (Dorland, 28th ed, p919)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:42',NULL,NULL,'4660FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1334,2802,'A protozoan disease caused by four species of the genus PLASMODIUM (P. falciparum (MALARIA, FALCIPARUM), P. vivax (MALARIA, VIVAX), P. ovale, and P. malariae) and transmitted by the bite of an infected female mosquito of the genus Anopheles. Malaria is endemic in parts of Asia, Africa, Central and South America, Oceania, and certain Caribbean islands. It is characterized by extreme exhaustion associated with paroxysms of high fever, sweating, shaking chills, and anemia.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:42',NULL,NULL,'4638FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1335,2804,'A malignant neoplasm derived from cells that are capable of forming melanin, which may occur in the skin of any part of the body, in the eye, or, rarely, in the mucous membranes of the genitalia, anus, oral cavity, or other sites. It occurs mostly in adults and may originate de novo or from a pigmented nevus or malignant lentigo. Melanomas frequently metastasize widely, and the regional lymph nodes, liver, lungs, and brain are likely to be involved. The incidence of malignant skin melanomas is rising rapidly in all parts of the world. (Stedman, 25th ed; from Rook et al., Textbook of Dermatology, 4th ed, p2445)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:43',NULL,NULL,'4605FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1336,2805,'A primary or metastatic malignant neoplasm involving the uterine corpus.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:43',NULL,NULL,'4602FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1337,2806,'Tumors or cancer of the endocrine glands in general or unspecified.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:43',NULL,NULL,'4600FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1338,2807,'Tumors or cancer of the pancreas.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:43',NULL,NULL,'4581FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1339,2808,'Tumors or cancer of the STOMACH.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:43',NULL,NULL,'4576FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1340,2810,'Cancer of the gums.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:44',NULL,NULL,'4561FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1341,2811,'Tumors or cancer of the LIP.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:44',NULL,NULL,'4558FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1342,2812,'Tumors or cancer of the SALIVARY GLANDS.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:44',NULL,NULL,'4551FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1343,2813,'Cancer or tumors of the bladder.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:44',NULL,NULL,'4532FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1344,2814,'Such malposition and contact of the maxillary and mandibular teeth as to interfere with the highest efficiency during the excursive movements of the jaw that are essential for mastication. (Jablonski, Illustrated Dictionary of Dentistry, 1982)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:45',NULL,NULL,'4528FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1345,2817,'A highly contagious infectious disease caused by MORBILLIVIRUS, common among children but also seen in the nonimmune of any age, in which the virus enters the respiratory tract via droplet nuclei and multiplies in the epithelial cells, spreading throughout the reticuloendothelial system. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:45',NULL,NULL,'4517FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1346,2819,'Syndrome caused by sucking of thick meconium into the lungs, usually by term or post-term infants (often small for gestational age) either in utero or with first breath. The resultant small airway obstruction may produce respiratory distress, tachypnea, cyanosis, pneumothorax, and/or pneumomediastinum.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:45',NULL,NULL,'4514FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1347,2823,'Disturbances in registering an impression, in the retention of an acquired impression, or in the recall of an impression. Memory impairments are associated with DEMENTIA; CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; ENCEPHALITIS; ALCOHOLISM (see also ALCOHOL AMNESTIC DISORDER); SCHIZOPHRENIA; and other conditions.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:46',NULL,NULL,'4504FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1348,2827,'Subnormal intellectual functioning which originates during the developmental period. This has multiple potential etiologies, including genetic defects and perinatal insults. Intelligence quotient (IQ) scores are commonly used to determine whether an individual is mentally retarded. IQ scores between 70 and 79 are in the borderline mentally retarded range. Scores below 67 are in the retarded range. (Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1992, Ch55, p28)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:47',NULL,NULL,'4487FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1349,2828,'Generic term for diseases caused by an abnormal metabolic process. It can be congenital due to inherited enzyme abnormality (METABOLISM, INBORN ERRORS) or acquired due to disease of an endocrine organ or failure of a metabolically important organ such as the liver. (Stedman, 26th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:47',NULL,NULL,'4485FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1350,2831,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:47',NULL,NULL,'4467FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1351,2832,'Abnormal protrusion of one or both of the leaflets of the mitral valve into the left atrium during systole. This may be accompanied by mitral regurgitation, systolic murmur, nonejection click, or cardiac arrhythmia.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:47',NULL,NULL,'4448FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1352,2836,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:48',NULL,NULL,'4445FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1353,2839,'Fractures in which the break in bone is not accompanied by an external wound.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:49',NULL,NULL,'4385FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1354,2843,'Form of leukemia characterized by an uncontrolled proliferation of the myeloid lineage and their precursors in the bone marrow and other sites.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:50',NULL,NULL,'4329FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1355,2845,'Gross necrosis of the myocardium, as a result of interruption of the blood supply to the area. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:50',NULL,NULL,'4326FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1356,2847,'Inflammation of the muscular walls of the heart. (Stedman, 25th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:50',NULL,NULL,'4324FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1357,2848,'A major deviation from normal patterns of behavior.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:50',NULL,NULL,'4312FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1358,2849,'A condition characterized by recurrent episodes of daytime somnolence and lapses in consciousness (microsomnias) that may be associated with automatic behaviors and AMNESIA. CATAPLEXY; SLEEP PARALYSIS, and hypnagogic HALLUCINATIONS frequently accompany narcolepsy. The pathophysiology of this disorder includes sleep-onset rapid eye movement (REM) sleep, which normally follows stage III or IV sleep. (From Neurology 1998 Feb;50(2 Suppl 1):S2-S7)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:51',NULL,NULL,'4310FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1359,2850,'Focal accumulations of edema fluid in the nasal mucosa accompanied by hyperplasia of the associated submucosal connective tissue. Polyps may be neoplasms, foci of inflammation, degenerative lesions, or malformations.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:51',NULL,NULL,'4306FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1360,2852,'A transient unconjugated hyperbilirubinemia that occurs between the second and fifth days of life because the hepatic enzyme GLUCURONOSYLTRANSFERASE required for BILIRUBIN detoxification is inadquedate.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:51',NULL,NULL,'4296FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1361,2856,'Neoplasms of the intracranial components of the central nervous system, including the cerebral hemispheres, basal ganglia, hypothalamus, thalamus, brain stem, and cerebellum. Brain neoplasms are subdivided into primary (originating from brain tissue) and secondary (i.e., metastatic) forms. Primary neoplasms are subdivided into benign and malignant forms. In general, brain tumors may also be classified by age of onset, histologic type, or presenting location in the brain.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:52',NULL,NULL,'4292FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1362,2858,'Clinical association of heavy proteinuria, hypoalbuminemia, and generalized edema.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:52',NULL,NULL,'4268FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1363,2862,'A general term indicating inflammation of a peripheral or cranial nerve. Clinical manifestation may include PAIN; PARESTHESIAS; PARESIS; or HYPESTHESIA.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:53',NULL,NULL,'4259FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1364,2863,'Diseases of the peripheral nerves external to the brain and spinal cord, which includes diseases of the nerve roots, ganglia, plexi, autonomic nerves, sensory nerves, and motor nerves.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:53',NULL,NULL,'4246FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1365,2865,'Failure or imperfection of vision at night or in dim light, with good vision only on bright days. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:53',NULL,NULL,'4240FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1366,2866,'Involuntary discharge of urine after the age at which urinary control should have been achieved; often used alone with specific reference to involuntary discharge of urine occurring during sleep at night (bed-wetting; nocturnal enuresis). (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:11:53',NULL,NULL,'4239FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
