(1414,2974,'Tuberculosis of the lungs.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:12',NULL,NULL,'3676FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1415,2975,'Purplish or brownish red discoloration, easily visible through the epidermis, caused by hemorrhage into the tissues.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:12',NULL,NULL,'3669FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1416,2977,'A cutaneous inflammatory reaction occurring as a result of exposure to ionizing radiation.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:12',NULL,NULL,'3661FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1417,2979,'Condition characterized by splenomegaly, some reduction in the number of circulating blood cells in the presence of a normal or hyperactive bone marrow, and the potential for reversal by splenectomy.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:12',NULL,NULL,'3652FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1418,2983,'The inability of a kidney to excrete metabolites at normal plasma levels under conditions of normal loading, or the inability to retain electrolytes under conditions of normal intake. In the acute form (KIDNEY FAILURE, ACUTE), it is marked by uremia and usually by oliguria or anuria, with hyperkalemia and pulmonary edema. The chronic form (KIDNEY FAILURE, CHRONIC) is irreversible and requires hemodialysis.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:13',NULL,NULL,'3639FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1419,2984,'A childhood seizure disorder characterized by rhythmic electrical brain discharges of geneneralized onset. Clinical features include a sudden cessation of ongoing activity usually without loss of postural tone. Rhythmic blinking of the eyelids or lip smacking frequently accompanies the seizure. The usual duration is 5-10 seconds, and multiple episodes may occur daily. Juvenile absence epilepsy is characterized by the juvenile onset of absence seizures and an increased incidence of myoclonus and tonic-clonic seizures. (Menkes, Textbook of Child Neurology, 5th ed, p736)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:13',NULL,NULL,'15623FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1420,2985,'Infection of the nose, sinuses, trachea (windpipe), bronchi, bronchioles or lungs.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:13',NULL,NULL,'3628FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1421,2991,'An acute, usually benign, infectious disease caused by the RUBELLA VIRUS and most often affecting children and nonimmune young adults, in which the virus enters the respiratory tract via droplet nuclei and spreads to the lymphatic system. (From Dorland, 27th edition)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:15',NULL,NULL,'3592FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1422,2992,'Sudden calamitous events producing great material damage, loss, and distress. They are the result of natural phenomena such as earthquakes, floods, etc.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:15',NULL,NULL,'15611FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1423,2996,'Disorders in which there is a loss of ego boundaries or a gross impairment in reality testing with delusions or prominent hallucinations. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:15',NULL,NULL,'3566FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1424,2997,'A personality disorder in which there are oddities of thought (magical thinking, paranoid ideation, suspiciousness), perception (illusions, depersonalization), speech (digressive, vague, overelaborate), and behavior (inappropriate affect in social interactions, frequently social isolation) that are not severe enough to characterize schizophrenia.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:16',NULL,NULL,'3564FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1425,2998,'A chronic, progressive dermatosis characterized by boardlike hardening and immobility of the affected skin, with visceral involvement, especially of lungs, esophagus, kidneys and heart. It may be accompanied by calcinosis, Raynaud&#39;s phenomenon, and telangiectasis (CREST syndrome). It includes acrosclerosis and sclerodactyly.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:16',NULL,NULL,'3557FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1426,2999,'Inflammation of the mucous membrane of the nose similar to that found in hay fever except that symptoms persist throughout the year. The causes are usually air-borne allergens, particularly dusts, feathers, molds, animal fur, etc.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:16',NULL,NULL,'3552FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1427,3000,'A chronic inflammatory disease of the skin of unknown etiology. It is characterized by moderate erythema, dry, moist, or greasy scaling, and yellow crusted patches on various areas, especially the scalp. On the scalp, it generally appears first as small patches of scales, progressing to involve the entire scalp with exfoliation of excessive amounts of dry scales (dandruff).','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:16',NULL,NULL,'3550FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1428,3002,'A general term referring to sudden and often violent motor activity of cerebral or brainstem origin. Convulsions may also occur in the absence of an electrical cerebral discharge (e.g., in response to hypotension).','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:17',NULL,NULL,'3527FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1429,3003,'Systemic disease associated with the presence and persistence of pathogenic microorganisms or their toxins in the blood. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:17',NULL,NULL,'3517FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1430,3005,'Infection of the nose, sinuses, trachea (windpipe), bronchi, bronchioles or lungs.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:17',NULL,NULL,'3513FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1431,3006,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-10-07 21:12:17',NULL,NULL,'3509FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
